{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/226565-changeling-the-dreaming-my-views-on-siochain","id":226565,"title":"Changeling: the Dreaming - My views on siochain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-12T16:45:08-07:00","id":226565,"title":"Changeling: the Dreaming - My views on siochain","content":"As I understand the duality between Yin and Yang, each one progresses into the other in an endless and harmonious cycle which continues the progression of the world. For instance you start with the Yin of lifeless soil which the Yang of vegetation grows from which in turn leads to the Yang of new soil when the vegetation once again dies.<br /> <br /> In a way we see the Yang of ambition and heroism leading to the Yin of struggle which leads back again to the Yang of triumph. Or studying science all your life and neglecting the glamorous side of existence can at times lead to world shaking wonders like vaccinations that saves millions and the discovery of the Higgs Boson. It seems to me that this could be a good example of the duality between Banality and Glamour, or the mortal world and the Dreaming, as each one depends on each other to complete the cycle that sustains each other and help each other to grow.<br /> <br /> What if a changeling who has attained siochain is one who has truely comprehended the need that the two worlds have for each other, seen the folly inherent in placing one above the other, and has learned to use their unique perspective to strengthen one another, and have adjusted their lives so that wonder leads to the healthy but monotonous labor which in turn leads to new Glamour which in turn inspires new labor, and in doing so have become something beyond merely mortal or Fae? What sort of mechanics besides agelessness should such beings have? Perhaps a slightly greater resistance to both Banality and Bedlam as they have assimilated within themselves the true nature of the Dreaming and the Autumn World? What should such beings be like? Would they start schools developed to teach their enlightenment or would they become recluses in Fae society? <br /> <br /> I would imagine they would spend most of their time in the Autumn World because that is where the greatest source of imbalance is, but perhaps they would travel to the societies built by the Fae in the Dreaming and try to convince them to return to Earth as a way of bringing new Glamour to the world. <br /> <br /> Another idea would be their take on the Unseelie/Seelie division. These enlightened beings would understand how one leads to the other and would be better able to understand how both could work together in tandem and be used to benefit the world around them. The Summer Court could be used as a court of nurturing new Dreamers and promoting positive social growth such as using their powers and influence to bring awareness to society of what needs to change and how it can be done. The point of the Summer Court would be to promote growth and nurturing in the hearts of mortals.<br /> <br /> The Winter Court, on the other hand, could be used as a more vigilante style tool of the Dreaming, doing everything from ecoterrorism, to acting as informents and even muses for law enforcement, always having just the right information and helping to inspire detectives to set up particularly successful stings in such matters as human trafficking and arms and drugs smuggling. Winter could still be into ravaging, but the Unseelie working under the Siochain could see that they should restrain themselves to people who actually deserve it like abusive pimps, human traffickers, organized crime members, Wall Street bankers, etc,.<br /> <br /> Ok, any thoughts? Also, were there ever any Changeling books that ever actually went into details concerning the Siochain? It seems 